<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4861" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμᾰθῖτις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιδος</span>,
			ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄμαθος</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>dwelling in sand,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. κόγχοι</span>
			<i>sand</i>-snails, <i><span class="en">
				Epich.
				42
			</span></i>. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄμᾰθος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰμ], ἡ,</span>
			
				Ep.
			 form of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄμμος,</span>
			<i>sand,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5.587
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.1239
			</span></i>, etc.: pl., <i>links, dunes</i> by the sea, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Ap.</u>
				439
			</span></i>; generally, <i>sandy soil,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				262
			</span></i>. (Dist. by Gramm., e.g. Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				9.384
			</span></i>, from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψάμμος</span> (q.v.) as
				<i>dust</i> from sea-sand, but prob.
				wrongly:—<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄμ-</span> is for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅμ-,</span> i. e. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σάμ-,</span> cf. <i>sand.</i>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
